## §15.4.11 — Cloudflare tunnel flap narrowed to the LOCAL PATH (COMM-08)
systemctl --user show cloudflared-alwayson.service -p NRestarts -p ActiveState
  ActiveState=active   NRestarts=1          <- unit state reports HEALTHY while flapping
Flap counts by window (grep -c 'Lost connection with the edge'):
  15 min ago: 0    1 hour ago: 26    6 hours ago: 121    24 hours ago: 384
Rate = 384 events over 204 distinct minutes => ~16/hour, one flap ~every 4 min.
  => NOT bursty. The "15 min ago: 0" sample is the misleading one.
Registered tunnel connections by PoP (24h):
  phx01 224, sjc01 59, sjc06 64, lax05 23, lax07 17, lax08 20, lax09 19, lax10 11, lax11 15
  distinct edge IPs = 4      transport = http2 on all 452 registrations
Loss counts per connection: connIndex 0/1/2/3 = 96/94/95/99 (near-identical)
  14 timestamps in last 6h carry >=3 simultaneous losses.
Route/reset/timeout signatures: 0
=> CONCLUSION: 3 independent PoPs cannot drop 4 connections in the same second.
   Fault is upstream of the PoP and common to all four => shared LOCAL path
   (uplink/NAT/host network path). NOT Cloudflare edge, NOT Mastodon, NOT unit state.
Prior session's attribution ("Cloudflare edge-to-tunnel hop") is RETRACTED — disproved above.
Origin clean: mastodon-web 5xx=0, mastodon-sidekiq 'error delivering'=0, queue:push_public=0
